
----------------------------------------
CyclicBarrier
--------------------------------------------
A CyclicBarrier is a synchronization tool in Java used when multiple
threads must wait for each other at a common point before all continue together.
Why Name “Cyclic”?
Because it can be reused again and again after threads cross the barrieer
------------------------------------------------
In Programming Meaning
3 threads doing work.
After finishing Step-1:
They must all wait.
When all reach barrier:
Then Step-2 starts together.
-------------------------------------------------------
Most Important Difference
CountDownLatch

Main thread waits for workers.

CyclicBarrier

Workers wait for each other.
CyclicBarrier = “Wait for your team, then move together.”
Best Real Example For You

3 developers deploying code:

Frontend ready
Backend ready
Database ready

When all ready → deploy together.